    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31721" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obluctātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		obluctor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a striving</i> or <i>struggling
				against, vehement opposition</i> (eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">obluctatio virtutis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Arn. 2, 77</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flammarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 6, § 647</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adversus mala,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 3, 11, 11</span></i>
			.—<i>Plur.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quis obluctationes sensit?</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ambros. Laps. Virg. 4, 12</span></i>
			.</div>
